**Proposition 20.5 (acquired choice, actual successor and resource
scope).** Compare the recovered entrance root coordinate with zero;
choose the leftmost current logical leaf if it is nonnegative and
the rightmost if negative. In earned code its type selects enabled
$P/S$. Execute that actual C call and retain the synchronized predictor.
Its actual successor field is

$$
T_{t'}\iota_gT_t^Ix.
\tag{20.8}
$$

The acquisition alone has $b(I+1)$ digital Reads, $I$ Ticks and no
Hold, Add, Reset or growth. The complete zero-alpha preparation and
assay has $I$ inner and $I$ outward growth transactions,
$b(I+1)$ Adds, $b(I+1)$ Reads and $3I$ Ticks, without Reset or Hold.

Proof. Finite exact root comparison and earned-code descent compute
an actual enabled leaf, without a selection oracle or new Tag port.
The real C adapter performs its new-tree Tick on the actual advanced
field, giving (20.8), and Theorem 7.2 follows it on all rational
successors. The acquisition counts follow its epoch schedule.
Canonical geometry has $I=n$ births, each with one attached Tick;
(20.7) has $b(I+1)$ literal Adds and $I$ Ticks; the assay has the
remaining $I$ Ticks and stated Reads. The selector call adds its own
inner/outward growth and one new-tree Tick. $\square$

Construction of $O,D$ and the routes has the conservative
$O(N^4)$ rational-work/$O(N^3)$-slot account of §13.
Equation (20.4) adds $O(NB)$ candidate arithmetic/gcd tests, not a
polynomial-in-$\ell(B)$ claim; reduction, comparison and copying use
actual operand widths. Unbounded numerators exclude a uniform
report/source-width bound in $N,B$. Geometry Ticks use their actual
intermediate sizes, and pulse/assay Ticks use the final tree size.
Producer ingress, pulses, providers, isolation and coexisting backing
remain paid.

The dense pulse/read family is sufficient, not minimum. An independent
row basis of $O$ permits a different square inverse and sparse
control/observation schedule, with its own pivot work, conditioning,
precision, largest epoch and return. No bill for that different
schedule is substituted above. Historical preparation is not closed
under arbitrary later Add, Reset or growth, and a later entrance need
not satisfy the old $B$. The current predictor remains valid there;
it does not replace the actual past by a new canonical Time.

